    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Description\n\nIn a wsl2 bash, issuing `:Git commit` from within neovim results in a timeout + sockconnect error after a few seconds.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nin a wsl2 bash:\r\n```\r\ngit init\r\ntouch a.txt\r\ngit add a.txt\r\nnvim -nu minimal.lua\r\n```\r\nin nvim:\r\n```\r\n:Git commit\r\n```\r\n\r\n[minimal.lua.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16334623/minimal.lua.zip)\r\n[version_info.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16334571/version_info.txt)\r\n[checkhealth.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16334560/checkhealth.txt)\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\ncommit message is opened for editing in existing nvim instance\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nerror with the following message is displayed:\r\n```\r\n(mini.git) PROCESS REACHED TIMEOUT\r\n(mini.git) Error detected while processing /tmp/nvim.stefan/erSj6H/0:\r\nline    6:\r\nE5108: Error executing lua Vim:connection failed: connection refused\r\nstack traceback:\r\n^I[C]: in function 'sockconnect'\r\n^I[string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```",
