        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the incredibly quick response!\r\n\r\nI did a bit more investigations after the hint about pipes. It seems that there is a discrepancy about pipe creation between platforms. On linux, nvim creates a pipe in /run/usr/*/nvim.proc*. On windows, nvim creates a pipe at \\\\.\\pipe\\nvim.*, on wsl it does not (v:servername is empty).\r\n\r\nHowever, pipes are workable on wsl2 too, the `:Git commit` command works fine when starting nvim giving a pipe name on command-line with `nvim -nu minimal.lua --listen /tmp/nvim-pipe`. Might be just the default pipe creation is missing in wsl2 build. But I believe that's not a topic for here.",
