        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Some more googling and experimenting revealed it's actually caused by a WSL bug with permissions/ownership of the run directory: https://github.com/microsoft/WSL/issues/11542, https://github.com/microsoft/WSL/issues/9689, and others. Nvim tries to create the pipe also on WSL but can't for permission problems - the directory where it wants to put the pipe is not accessible.\r\n\r\nNothing at all wrong with the plugin, I guess this can be closed. Sorry for the wrong report, and thanks for the hint with the pipes.",
